@startuml DR-010-arch-target_component
title Target picture: mw::com first, one forwarding path, one daemon service interface\nGrouped by owning repository

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor<<ASIL-B>> #FFE6E6
  BackgroundColor<<QM>> #E6F0FF
  BackgroundColor<<external>> #F2F2F2
  BackgroundColor<<open>> #FFF8DC
  BackgroundColor<<retired>> #D9D9D9
}

package "Application repos (integrator)" as APPS {
  component "Application A\n(mw::com API)" as AppA
  component "Application B\n(mw::com API)" as AppB
}

package "eclipse-score/communication (mw::com core and interfaces)" as COM {
  component "LoLa binding\n(zero-copy, same host)" as Lola
  component "Binding interface (SPI)\nand build-time binding table" as Spi
  component "Serializer plugin API\n(implementations: open)" as SerApi
  component "Forwarding\n(generic proxy, transport,\nskeleton; from mw::com gateway)" as Fwd
  component "Daemon service IF\n(mw::com services)" as DIF
}

package "eclipse-score/inc_someip_gateway (SOME/IP protocol repository)" as GWR {
  component "SOME/IP binding\n(library; package location open)" as SomeBind
  component "gatewayd\n(ASIL-B: E2E, policy, ACL, config;\nno forwarding code of its own)" as GW <<ASIL-B>>
  component "socom\n(retired, replaced by Daemon service IF)" as Socom <<retired>>
  component "someipd\n(stack daemon, one per host)" as SomeIPD <<QM>> {
    component "SOME/IP-SD and protocol\n(behind Daemon service IF)" as Proto <<QM>>
    component "Transport plugin\n(sockets)" as Sock <<QM>>
    component "Transport plugin\n(io-sock fast path, optional)" as Fast <<QM>>
  }
}

package "DDS repo (open decision)" as DDSR {
  component "DDS binding\n(library)" as DdsBind
  component "ddsd\n(DDS Communication Daemon, one per host)" as DDSD <<QM>> {
    component "DDS integration\n(behind DDS IF)" as DDSI <<QM>>
  }
}

package "External and candidate stacks" as EXT {
  component "lg-someip\n(candidate for someipd;\nlocation open)" as LG <<open>>
  component "opensomeip\n(candidate for someipd,\nPR #435)" as OSI <<open>>
  component "io-sock (QNX)" as IOS <<external>>
  component "Cyclone DDS" as CYC <<external>>
}

cloud "Vehicle network" as Net

AppA --> Lola : same host
AppA --> SomeBind : direct placement
Lola --> AppB : same host

Lola ..|> Spi
SomeBind ..|> Spi
DdsBind ..|> Spi

GW --> Fwd : forwards events
Fwd --> Lola : local side
Fwd --> SomeBind : remote side
Fwd --> DdsBind : remote side (DDS)
GW --> SerApi : payload
SomeBind --> SerApi : payload
DdsBind --> SerApi : payload

SomeBind --> DIF : daemon service IF
DdsBind --> DIF : daemon service IF
DIF --> SomeIPD : daemon service IF
DIF --> DDSD : daemon service IF

Socom ..> DIF : replaced by

Proto ..> LG : links (candidate)
Proto ..> OSI : links (candidate)
Proto --> Sock : transport IF
Proto ..> Fast : optional, per route
Fast ..> IOS : kernel sockets
DDSI ..> CYC : links

Sock --> Net
Fast --> Net
DDSI --> Net

note bottom of COM
  D1 mw::com first. Same host: LoLa.
     Other ECU: a SOME/IP or DDS binding from
     its protocol repository, placed in the app
     or in gatewayd.
  D2 One forwarding path, here.
  D3 Daemon service IF on mw::com; socom retired
     once mw::com has generic methods
     (communication#767).
  D6 Serializer plugin API here.
end note

note bottom of GWR
  D4 gatewayd only for apps that cannot use mw::com
     directly, and for central E2E and policy.
  D5 One protocol daemon per protocol per host.
     Protocol logic only in the daemon.
  D7 io-sock fast path optional until measured.
  P6 ASIL-B processes never link a protocol stack.
end note

note bottom of EXT
  Stack choice is decided by the Q1 measurements.
  Build-time dependency of someipd only.
end note

note bottom of APPS
  Bindings are build-time dependencies of the
  binary that uses them (P5). Nothing is
  registered or loaded after startup.
  Specs and decisions: eclipse-score/score.
end note
@enduml
